# MadGraph5 batch script: u u~ > e+ e- g at LO, QCD=2 QED=2.
#
# One concrete flavour assignment out of the `q q~ > l+ l- g` class of
# `p p > l+ l- j QCD=2 QED=2` (MadGraph's P1_qq_llg group), so the matrix
# element is matrix1 and a per-diagram AMP dump means one diagram per row.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The baseline of a three-point design over the llj subprocess classes:
#     u u~ > e+ e- g (here), g u > e+ e- u (colour arrangement varied) and
#     d d~ > e+ e- g (initial flavour varied). Each partner changes exactly one
#     variable against this row, so a disagreement localises.
#   - A gluon radiated off an annihilating quark line: the single colour
#     structure T^a_{ij} (NCOLOR=1), with the gluon attaching either before or
#     after the electroweak vertex. The two attachments differ by the sign of
#     the internal quark propagator's momentum, which is where a fermion-flow
#     or spine-parity convention error shows up per diagram while |M|^2 stays
#     unmoved only if both signs are wrong together.
#
# lpp=0 => fixed-energy partonic beams, so `launch` integrates sigma-hat and
# builds matrix1_optim.f (the |M|^2 oracle) alongside matrix1_orig.f (the
# per-diagram AMP oracle).
generate u u~ > e+ e- g QCD=2 QED=2
output uux_to_epemg -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
